kavaugha@gmail.com wrote:
> I'm new to nethack and have a couple of very basic questions for the
> game...
> - Is there an easy way to destroy boulders? I often find myself with
> no choice but to push them in front of me and end up blocking my path
> to the next level.

To destroy boulders (which is not the only way to circumvent them) you
may use digging tools (pickaxes, mattocks AKA bload picks), wands of
striking, spells of force bolt. You may also teleport away the boulder
using some wand or spell. You may squeeze past a boulder if you are
sufficiently stripped and with not too much objects in your inventory.
You may also dig down (pickaxe, wand of digging) to the next level or
level teleport to the next level (confused teleport scroll, or cursed
teleport scroll) but you should have some way of teleport control (ring).

> - How do I invoke the search function? The guidebook mentions a search
> function that reveals traps and secret doors/passages, and I haven't
> been able to use it. Is there another way to find there apart from
> walking into them? Also, are there any ways to light up dark rooms?
> thanks

The search command is 's'; it requires usually a couple of moves (10-20
just to name some not unusual numbers) to be effective. Wearing a ring
of searching (or the artifact weapon Excalibur) will reduce the number
of turns until you find something. Passages may also be detected by a
stethoscope applied once in the respective direction. Wands of secret
door detection will (just to name a more common way) will also reveal
traps and passages.

To light up dark rooms temporarily; there are assorted lamps (best chance
to find one is in the lighting store in Minetown), worse are candles, and
if you're happy to have got the Sunsword it will also give you permanent
light whereever you move (as does a specific magic lamp). To lighten an
area permanently; this is done by a scroll of light, a spell of light, or
a wand of light.

Of course you need to have those items described. If not, be creative :-)
In Nethack there are often more ways to achieve something.

